WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.367 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
Where did this answer come from?

2
00:00:03.633 --> 00:00:07.833 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
One question captures the challenge of trust in Islamic knowledge.

3
00:00:07.867 --> 00:00:12.600 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
Qaf brings questions and sources closer together.

4
00:00:13.667 --> 00:00:16.667 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
Qaf helps researchers and readers explore a question,

5
00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:19.200 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
and read cited passages in their context.

6
00:00:19.233 --> 00:00:24.233 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
Books, authors, and source locations remain alongside the answer.

7
00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:30.467 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
Jev. An experimental workflow that selects evidence before writing.

8
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:34.267 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
It classifies the question and evaluates the retrieved passages,

9
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.200 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
then reviews coverage and identifies the gaps.

10
00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:40.800 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
Code controls the follow-up steps.

11
00:00:40.833 --> 00:00:44.000 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
Gemini then writes from a numbered evidence pack.

12
00:00:44.033 --> 00:00:47.933 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
Citation numbers resolve to known passages the reader can inspect.

13
00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:53.267 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
In the independent educational demo, we ask: how do we check a quotation?

14
00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:58.067 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
We open a citation and see the passage advising us to read the surrounding sentences.

15
00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:01.133 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
When evidence is missing, the demo states its limits.

16
00:01:02.333 --> 00:01:06.700 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
In a previous study using 48 questions,

17
00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:10.667 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
estimated mean cost was about 40% lower.

18
00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:14.133 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
Median time to the first readable answer text fell

19
00:01:14.167 --> 00:01:18.667 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
from about thirteen seconds to less than ten.

20
00:01:19.833 --> 00:01:22.833 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
No quality advantage has been established:

21
00:01:22.867 --> 00:01:27.333 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
Twenty preferences for the experimental workflow, sixteen for production,

22
00:01:27.367 --> 00:01:31.067 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
and twelve undecided comparisons.

23
00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:34.933 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
The study predates the challenge, and its evaluation is automated.

24
00:01:34.967 --> 00:01:37.200 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
In the audit sample, serious errors were found

25
00:01:37.233 --> 00:01:39.933 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
in six of eighteen answers in each workflow.

26
00:01:41.067 --> 00:01:47.867 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
The submission provides an independent explanation and a demo with synthetic data,

27
00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:50.833 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
with documented results and limitations.

28
00:01:50.867 --> 00:01:55.067 line:78% position:50% align:center size:85%
Qaf. A clearer question. Evidence closer at hand.
